  <div class="dossier-content"><p class="eyebrow">01 / PERSONAL DOSSIER</p><h1>Behind the <em>interface.</em></h1><p class="lead">A student of systems. A builder of connections.</p>
  <div class="profile-grid"><div class="body-copy"><p>I'm Michel Deosaran, a Computing & Information Systems undergraduate at Athabasca University. I enjoy understanding how complex systems work, and how software and business come together to solve real problems.</p><p>At Zeon Michael Group, I work on practical problems at the grassroots level, exploring how software can make personal finance and small businesses work better. That means building useful tools, managing data pipelines, and turning ideas into solutions grounded in people's everyday needs.</p><p>My studies cover networking, operating systems, programming, databases, and cloud technologies. I've also gotten hands-on with real estate data and quantitative finance, putting what I learn into practice through data workflows, financial modelling, and software projects.</p><p>Beyond computing, I enjoy learning languages. I completed French Immersion bilingual studies and study Japanese through The Japan Foundation, Toronto.</p></div><aside class="profile-facts"><span class="eyebrow">FOCUS AREAS</span><h3>Computing</h3><p>Python · JavaScript · SQL<br />Linux · Bash · Docker<br />PostgreSQL · MySQL</p><h3>Business development</h3><p>Outreach · CRM · Research<br />Communication · Sales strategy</p><a class="enter-button" href="/contact/">LET'S CONNECT <span>↗</span></a></aside></div></div>
</Layout>
